## Don't forget the overlay

Appended data sits outside every section, so section-walking tools skip it entirely:

```python
end = max(s.PointerToRawData + s.SizeOfRawData for s in pe.sections)
print(f"last section ends 0x{end:x}, file is 0x{len(data):x}, overlay = {len(data)-end}")
```

One correction to make before you get excited: if the binary is Authenticode-signed, the signature blob lives in the overlay. Subtract it — `pe.OPTIONAL_HEADER.DATA_DIRECTORY[4]` gives its offset and size. Whatever's left over after that is genuine appended data.

